Description: Frida 17.19.0 for RootHide
 The official frida-server, repackaged so RootHide can install it.
 .
 Nothing here is rebuilt. build.frida.re publishes rootful and
 rootless builds but no RootHide one, so RootHide users are stuck on
 frida 16 while Dopamine 3.0.10 (iOS 26) wants 17.19.0 or newer.
 .
 The rootful build already carries what RootHide needs: frida-server
 is fat with an arm64e slice at capabilities 0x80, frida-agent is
 arm64 + arm64e, and neither bakes in a path. The only thing missing
 is a three-line wrapper that points CRYPTEX_MOUNT_PATH at the jbroot,
 plus a package architecture dpkg will accept. That is all this is.
 .
 Every build re-checks the arm64e slice: if upstream ever drops it,
 packaging stops rather than shipping something that cannot run.
 .
 frida 17 removed the global ObjC bridge and Module.getExportByName.
 shivtools agents are compiled with the bridge embedded, so they run
 on both 16 and 17. Your own agents need:
 frida-compile <agent>.js -B iife -S -o <out>.js
