Description: Node.js 24.21.0 with npm, patched for iOS
 Node 24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, npx and corepack. Everything is in the
 package: nothing is downloaded or compiled when you install it.
 .
 Node is not cross-compiled. This is the official darwin-arm64 build
 from nodejs.org, verified against the checksum nodejs.org publishes,
 then rewritten to claim platform iOS and linked against a shim that
 supplies the three symbols iOS lacks. The shim is also what makes V8
 run: iOS rejects MAP_JIT and has no pthread_jit_write_protect_np, so
 it keeps each page of V8's code ranges writable or executable and
 repairs the fault when a thread needs the other.
 .
 The patch and the shim are andi's work (MIT), from
 github.com/realAndi/nodejs-for-ios. What is different here: the
 binary is patched and signed at build time instead of on the device,
 so installing needs no network, no free gigabyte and no python3,
 ldid, curl or tar. Built for both rootless and RootHide.
 .
 npm install -g writes to ~/.npm-global, per user, without sudo.
 .
 Needs an A12 chip or newer. Prebuilt native addons (.node) do not
 load. Node 24 and newer only; 23 and earlier cannot be patched.
