Description: terminal AI assistant
 shiv is a chat assistant that runs entirely in your terminal.
 Nothing else to install - Node.js ships inside the package.
 .
 Sign in to OpenRouter from the browser: /login opens the approval
 page, you confirm with your account and the key comes back - no
 copying keys by hand. Or paste your own key for DeepSeek, OpenAI,
 Moonshot, xAI, Qwen, Z.ai, Groq, Mistral, Together, a local
 Ollama / llama.cpp, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
 .
 It reads files, searches directories and runs shell commands,
 asking before anything that could modify your device. Sessions
 are saved and can be resumed, and there is a rewind that takes
 the conversation back to an earlier point.
 .
 For tweak work it measures the device instead of guessing: /env
 reports theos, frida, oldabi and the tools it found. Bundled
 helpers dump ObjC classes from the dyld cache or from a live app,
 and decrypt an App Store binary on the device itself.
 .
 Drawing and streaming speed can be tuned from /performance, so
 it stays responsive in long sessions. Interface is Turkish or
 English (/lang). Separate builds for rootless and RootHide.
